---
// Root redirects to the default locale instantly. This page has no content of
// its own; it exists only to forward.
//
// Signalling rules (both learned the hard way — do not "harden" this again):
//  - canonical points at the redirect target, and is absolute. A relative
//    "/zh/" also resolves correctly per spec; absolute is chosen only to remove
//    any ambiguity about the base, not because relative was broken.
//  - NO robots noindex here. Google treats noindex + rel=canonical as
//    contradictory: the canonical asks to consolidate into /zh/ while noindex
//    asks to drop a page, and the documented failure mode is that the canonical
//    is ignored or the whole cluster (including /zh/) is dropped. Exclusion of
//    this stub is handled where it is unambiguous — the sitemap filter in
//    astro.config.mjs — not by stacking a second, conflicting directive.
const target = new URL('/zh/', Astro.site).href;
---

<!doctype html>
<html>
  <head>
    <meta charset="utf-8" />
    <meta http-equiv="refresh" content={`0;url=${target}`} />
    <link rel="canonical" href={target} />
    <title>Atlas for Mac</title>
  </head>
  <body></body>
</html>
